From 34015904824e4811b7c5c08a215c92ec2de79a1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Thomas <chris.thomas@antimatter-studios.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 09:30:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(desktop): per-key agent policy, app/data lock split, and
 a reworked layout
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Unlocking a vault used to freeze the window: every `#[tauri::command]` was
synchronous, so it ran on the main thread and blocked the event loop for the
whole Argon2 derivation. All sixteen commands now run off the main thread and
the unlock reports its progress step by step instead of going dark.

Locking is now two separate ideas, because one button was doing both:

- App lock hides the window. It takes nothing back from the machine, and it
  fires on the idle timer.
- Data lock removes that vault's keys from the system agent and dematerializes
  its files. It applies to one database, so with several open you land on the
  next open vault rather than at a login screen.

Each SSH entry gets its own agent policy — whether to load it, how long it
lives, whether to confirm each signature, and whether a data lock takes it
back — written to KeeAgent.settings so KeePassXC reads the same values.

The toolbar row is gone. Search moved above the list it filters, the lock
state onto the vault chip that it describes, and the app controls to the top
of the detail column. The title bar carries the vault name, the key count and
expiry, and the build stamp.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014AdM94sGw7X5A2qPLtVXyk
